# zerobas is a Unix-toolchain project (GNU make + pasmo + python3, driven through a
# /bin/sh-style shell even on Windows via MSYS2). Force LF in every working tree so
# the Makefile recipes and the assembled sources are never broken by CRLF — the
# GitHub Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true otherwise, which appends
# a stray \r to every make recipe line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never apply end-of-line conversion or text diffing (it would
# corrupt them). The .ips/.bps patch deliverables are tracked; the rest may appear
# as build outputs, test images, or oracle captures.
*.ips binary
*.bps binary
*.rom binary
*.dsk binary
*.bin binary
*.wav binary
*.cas binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
